// Title: Suspicious Executable File Creation
// Sigma ID: 74babdd6-a758-4549-9632-26535279e654
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-09-05 | Modified: 2023-12-11
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564
// Description: Detect creation of suspicious executable file names. Some strings look for suspicious file
//   extensions, others look for filenames that exploit unquoted service paths.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://medium.com/@SumitVerma101/windows-privilege-escalation-part-1-unquoted-service-path-c7a011a8d8ae
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/76c69e2d-01e8-49d9-9aea-fb7cc0c4d3ad/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_executable_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith ":\\$Recycle.Bin.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\Documents and Settings.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\MSOCache.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\PerfLogs.exe" or FolderPath endswith ":\\Recovery.exe" or FolderPath endswith ".bat.exe" or FolderPath endswith ".sys.exe"
